<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 April, from 796 to 1955.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">796 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Æthelred I of Northumbria is murdered</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Æthelred I was killed at Corbridge by his own nobles. His death, typical of Northumbria's violent politics, came three years after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raiders had sacked the monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferrara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1428">1428 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">598 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Peace of Ferrara ends a campaign of the Wars in Lombardy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the mediation of the Pope, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and the Gonzaga signed a peace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a>, ending the second campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-in-lombardy">Wars in Lombardy</a>. Venice kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> and gained Bergamo, and Florence recovered strongholds it had lost.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-in-lombardy">Wars in Lombardy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1506">1506 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius II lays the foundation stone of the new St Peter's</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> laid the first stone of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donato-bramante">Bramante</a>'s new basilica in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Building took 120 years and drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>, Maderno and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini">Bernini</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1689">1689 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">337 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Boston revolts against the Dominion of New England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militia and citizens in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>, prompted by news of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a>, rose against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Sir Edmund Andros</a>, governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a>, and arrested dominion officials. Leaders of the former Massachusetts Bay Colony then reclaimed the government.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul Revere rides to warn of British troops</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Paul Revere and William Dawes rode from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> to warn that British regulars were marching to seize colonial arms. The first shots of the Revolutionary War were fired at dawn the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1906">1906 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">120 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and fire devastate San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake struck before dawn, and fires burned for three days. Some 3,000 people died and more than half the city's population was left homeless.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yankee Stadium opens with a Babe Ruth home run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Babe Ruth hit a three-run home run in the first game at the new Bronx ballpark, quickly nicknamed 'The House That Ruth Built'. It was home to the Yankees until 2008.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein dies in Princeton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein">Albert Einstein</a> died aged 76. His theories of special and general relativity and his work on light quanta transformed physics in the twentieth century.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 April <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kan-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kan-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">K'an II</span><span class="tp">588–658</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lucrezia-borgia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lucrezia-borgia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lucrezia Borgia</span><span class="tp">1480–1519</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-ricardo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-ricardo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David Ricardo</span><span class="tp">1772–1823</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</span><span class="tp">1819–1874</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jaan-anvelt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jaan-anvelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jaan Anvelt</span><span class="tp">1884–1937</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tatya-tope"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Tatya Tope</span><span class="tp">1814–1859</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/justus-von-liebig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/justus-von-liebig.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Justus von Liebig</span><span class="tp">1803–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oscar-carmona"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oscar-carmona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Óscar Carmona</span><span class="tp">1869–1951</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-einstein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Einstein</span><span class="tp">1879–1955</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
